  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "Playing passback in smashball taught you the importance of making good throws under pressure. When using a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Thrown_Weapon\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Thrown Weapon\">Thrown Weapon</a>, you can <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Aim\" title=\"Aim\">Aim</a> with a single <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a> instead of two. Additionally, you can benefit from <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Aiming\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Aiming\">Aiming</a> with a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Thrown_Weapon\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Thrown Weapon\">Thrown Weapon</a> even if the weapon makes an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Area_Attack\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Area Attack\">Area Attack</a>. When using this <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Talents\" title=\"Talents\">Talent</a>, you do not gain the benefits of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Deadeye\" title=\"Deadeye\">Deadeye</a> <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Feats\" title=\"Feats\">Feat</a> if the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ranged_Weapons\" title=\"Ranged Weapons\">Thrown Weapon</a> is making an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Area_Attacks\" title=\"Area Attacks\">Area Attack</a>.",
